{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-65298","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95515","text":"Graphonomous FAQ"}]},{"id":"blk-65299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95516","text":"This page answers the most common questions about Graphonomous, its MCP interface, and operating model."}]},{"id":"blk-65300","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95517","text":"What is Graphonomous?"}]},{"id":"blk-65301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95518","text":"Graphonomous is a continual-learning memory engine for AI agents. It stores knowledge as a graph, supports confidence-updating feedback loops, and exposes all capabilities through MCP tools/resources."}]},{"id":"blk-65302","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95519","text":"Does Graphonomous retrain model weights?"}]},{"id":"blk-65303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95520","text":"No. Graphonomous does "},{"id":"spn-95521","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-95522","text":" retrain model weights. Learning happens in the memory graph by storing knowledge and updating confidence based on outcomes."}]},{"id":"blk-65304","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95523","text":"What problem does it solve?"}]},{"id":"blk-65305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95524","text":"It gives agents durable, evolving memory and better decision quality over time by combining:"}]},{"id":"blk-65306","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95525","text":"semantic retrieval"}]}],"id":"blk-65307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95526","text":"graph neighborhood expansion"}]}],"id":"blk-65309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95527","text":"causal outcome feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-65311","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95528","text":"goal tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-65313","kind"